OL,3,GNEWSASea swimmers 'taking control' of
OL,4,Awater quality tests
OL,5,
OL,6,FSea swimmers in Worthing say they are
OL,7,F"taking control" of water quality and
OL,8,Fholding Southern Water "to account" by
OL,9,Fcarrying out their own seawater tests.
OL,11,FThe Environment Agency (EA) currently
OL,12,Ftests designated bathing waters between
OL,13,FMay and September, but Mark Smith from
OL,14,FMuscle Beach Swimming Club would like
OL,15,Fto see it happen all year round.
OL,17,FNow, three sea swimming clubs in the
OL,18,Ftown have been given equipment to test
OL,19,Ffor levels of harmful E. coli bacteria
OL,20,Foften found in raw sewage.
OL,23,APub: 19-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,329,320,200,140,0,100
